---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PosterBand from "../components/PosterBand.astro";
import { SITE } from "../data/site";
---

<Base path="/privacy/">
  <PosterBand path="/privacy/">
    <Fragment slot="title">Your information.<br /><em>Your choices.</em></Fragment>
    <p slot="intro">This notice covers the Break the Bonds | Arkansas website and its campaign contact links.</p>
  </PosterBand>

  <div class="wrap privacy">
    <div class="prose">
      <section aria-labelledby="hosting-title">
        <h2 id="hosting-title">Website hosting</h2>
        <p>
          Cloudflare hosts this site. It processes requests for the site’s pages and files in order to serve them. Some
          browsers may also send Cloudflare a report when a request to the site fails or returns an error. This site does not
          set cookies.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Read Cloudflare’s privacy policy</a> for details about collection,
          use, sharing, and retention.
        </p>
        <p>
          No statistics, analytics, or tracking resources load during visits to this site, and no resources load from any other
          website. Reading a page or downloading a document does not require sending the campaign your name or email address.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="contacting-title">
        <h2 id="contacting-title">Contacting the campaign</h2>
        <p>
          Campaign contact links open your email application. The website does not send an email for you. If you choose to
          write, the campaign receives your email address and the information you include.
        </p>
        <p>
          To ask about information you have shared with the campaign, or request a correction or deletion, email <a
            href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>breakbondsar@proton.me</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="signup-title">
        <h2 id="signup-title">The sign-up form</h2>
        <p>
          The sign-up form on the Take action page asks for your name and email address. You can also give a phone number, a ZIP
          code, the ways you want to help, and a short note.
        </p>
        <p>
          When you press Sign up, the site stores what you entered in a Cloudflare D1 database kept for the campaign. With it,
          the site stores the date and time, the path of the page you sent it from, and a one-way code made from your browser’s
          user-agent string, which helps the campaign spot repeated or automated sign-ups. Your IP address is not stored.
          Cloudflare uses it to count the sign-ups sent from each address over one-minute periods, so one connection cannot send
          many at once. If you sign up again with the same email address, your earlier sign-up is updated.
        </p>
        <p>
          The campaign uses these details to contact you about its work. It does not sell them or share them with anyone. To see,
          correct, or delete your sign-up, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>breakbondsar@proton.me</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="tools-title">
        <h2 id="tools-title">Action tools and outside links</h2>
        <p>
          The copy buttons place the displayed message or discussion prompts on your clipboard only when you press them. They do
          not send a message or submit anything to a public office.
        </p>
        <p>
          Links to public offices, source documents, Instagram, and other websites take you to those services. Their own privacy
          practices apply. The campaign’s font files are served from this website.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="updates-title">
        <h2 id="updates-title">Updates</h2>
        <p>This notice will be updated if the website’s features or information practices change.</p>
        <p class="provenance">Last reviewed: October 19, 2026.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="records-title">
        <h2 id="records-title">Records and contact choices</h2>
        <p>
          You can read the records and download the ledger without submitting information to the campaign. Email and the sign-up form are optional.
          Avoid including banking details, identity documents, or other sensitive information when reporting an error or asking
          to join.
        </p>
        <p>
          Campaign correspondence is used to respond to the message and discuss the next step you request. Questions about
          access, correction, deletion, or how your correspondence is handled can be sent to the campaign contact above.
        </p>
        <p>
          The public evidence archive uses reviewed copies with private contact and account details removed. Public investment
          identifiers identify securities; they are not personal bank-account numbers.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .privacy {
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-8);
  }
  .privacy section {
    margin-top: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .privacy section > * + * {
    margin-top: 0.8em;
  }
  .privacy h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }
</style>
